feov-record: a command was named and the surface is scoped to whoever is asking.

--seat-id IS REQUIRED HERE, because nothing identified you: this agent has not registered, so the record cannot say which seat it holds, and no --seat-id was given. The surface is scoped to whoever is asking, so there is no tree to show until you say who that is — a seat id, or `operator`. You type it ONCE, at `register`; after that the binding is on the record and every later call resolves it for you.

feov-record — the seat-side record runtime (the verb set IS the role boundary)

A lens structurally cannot mint or close a board gap: no such verb exists in its
namespace. Blue has no board verbs at all. The bench rules and never originates.

